<config xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:module:Magento_Config:etc/system_file.xsd">
    <system>
        <tab id="adpage" sortOrder="999" translate="label">
            <label>AdPage</label>
        </tab>
        <section id="GTM" translate="label" sortOrder="342" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
            <label>AdPage GTM</label>
            <tab>adpage</tab>
            <resource>Tagging_GTM::config</resource>
            <group id="settings" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="1" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                <label>Settings</label>
                <field id="enabled" type="select" translate="label" sortOrder="1" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Enabled</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                </field>
                <field id="config" translate="label" sortOrder="2" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Container HEAD code</label>
                    <comment>Container Head code which can be found in the trytagging dashboard. Be sure to select "Magento" as platform else the code will not work.</comment>
                    <frontend_model>Tagging\GTM\Model\Config\Frontend\ContainerConfig</frontend_model>
                    <backend_model>Tagging\GTM\Model\Config\Backend\ContainerConfig</backend_model>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="lifetime_value" type="select" translate="label" sortOrder="3" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Include lifetime value</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="serverside_gtm_url" type="text" translate="label" sortOrder="3" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Container URL</label>
                    <comment><![CDATA[<span>Enter the container url without https://<span><br/>
                    <b>Keep in mind</b>; This must much with the container config you are installing. ]]></comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="debug" type="select" translate="label" sortOrder="4" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Debug</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="choose_script_placement" type="select" translate="label" sortOrder="5" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Choose script placement</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment><![CDATA[<span>If you want to control on where the scripts are placed you can enable this option. Then the plugin will not load the files and you have to do it on your own.<span><br/>
                    <b>NOTE</b>; If all necessary scripts are not included, tracking will not function. ]]></comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="price_visibility" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="2" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                <label>Price visibility</label>
                <field id="enabled" type="select" translate="label" sortOrder="1" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Hide prices in the dataLayer</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment><![CDATA[Enable this on B2B stores that only show prices to logged in customers. The prices of the
                    selected customer groups are then also kept out of the dataLayer, so they are not readable in the
                    page source or in the browser console.<br/>
                    <b>NOTE</b>; Order data on the success page and in the <i>order_created</i> webhook always keeps its
                    real amounts, otherwise revenue reporting would break.]]></comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="*/settings/enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="customer_groups" type="multiselect" translate="label" sortOrder="2" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Hide prices for customer groups</label>
                    <source_model>Tagging\GTM\Model\Config\Source\CustomerGroups</source_model>
                    <comment>Visitors in these customer groups get no prices in the dataLayer. Select "NOT LOGGED IN" to hide prices from guests.</comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="*/settings/enabled">1</field>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="mode" type="select" translate="label" sortOrder="3" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Hide prices by</label>
                    <source_model>Tagging\GTM\Model\Config\Source\HidePriceMode</source_model>
                    <comment>Leaving the price out is the cleanest option. Choose "Send the price as 0" when your GTM container expects the price and value keys to always be present.</comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="*/settings/enabled">1</field>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="advanced" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="3" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                <label>Advanced Settings</label>
                <attribute type="expanded">0</attribute>
                <field id="webhook_trigger_mode" type="select" translate="label" sortOrder="1" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Change webhook trigger</label>
                    <comment>Choose how the purchase webhook should be triggered</comment>
                    <source_model>Tagging\GTM\Model\Config\Source\WebhookTriggerOptions</source_model>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="*/settings/enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="webhook_trigger_order_state" type="text" translate="label" sortOrder="2" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Order state for webhook trigger</label>
                    <comment><![CDATA[Enter the order state that should trigger the webhook.<br/>
                    <b>Example Magento order states:</b> pending_payment, processing, complete, closed, canceled, holded, payment_review]]></comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="*/settings/enabled">1</field>
                        <field id="webhook_trigger_mode">on_order_state</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
            </group>
        </section>
    </system>
</config>
